---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import { business, plan, money } from '../data/business';
import { organizationSchema } from '../data/schema';
import { orderHref } from '../data/order';
const audit = plan('audit');
const foundation = plan('foundation');
const maintain = plan('maintain');
const orgSchema = organizationSchema(Astro.site);
---
<Base title="Wardith — Be part of the answer" description="Find out whether AI assistants recommend your business, and what is getting in the way. Independent written audit: £250. UK service businesses.">
  <section class="new-hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="section-label">AI visibility for UK service businesses</p>
        <h1>Your customers<br />are asking AI.<br /><em>Are you in<br class="desktop-break" /> the answer?</em></h1>
        <p class="hero-intro">Wardith checks whether AI assistants recommend your business, explains what they find, and helps you fix what’s getting in the way.</p>
        <a class="btn" href={orderHref}>Explore your {money(audit.price)} audit <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <p class="micro">A written report. Yours to keep. No ongoing commitment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <div class="question-card"><span class="question-label">A potential customer asks</span><p>“Who would you recommend<br />for a service like yours?”</p><span class="question-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
        <figure class="answer-diagram">
          <figcaption><span>From question to shortlist</span><span class="diagram-index">01 / 02</span></figcaption>
          <div class="answer-heading">A few names.<br /><em>One opportunity.</em></div>
          <div class="answer-list" aria-label="Illustration of a shortlist, not actual AI results">
            <div><span class="answer-number">01</span><span>A business they discover</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
            <div class="your-business"><span class="answer-number">02</span><span>Could this be you?</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
            <div><span class="answer-number">03</span><span>Another name to consider</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="diagram-note">Illustration only. Answers vary by assistant, question and time.</p>
        </figure>
        <a class="visual-foot" href="/ask-your-ai/">See how to check for yourself <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="wrap assistant-strip"><span>The places we look</span><div><span>ChatGPT</span><span>Google</span><span>Copilot</span><span>Perplexity</span></div></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section audit-section" id="the-audit">
    <div class="wrap audit-grid">
      <div class="audit-copy"><p class="section-label">The starting point</p><h2>See what your<br />customers see.</h2><p>You shouldn’t have to guess why another business gets mentioned. The audit records the answers and checks the information behind them.</p><p>You receive a plain-English report with the evidence and a recommendation on what to do next. If further work isn’t worth buying, it says so.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/">Inside the audit <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><div class="audit-facts"><div><strong>{money(audit.price)}</strong><span>One-off price</span></div><div><strong>2 working days</strong><span>After scope and payment are confirmed</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="report-preview" aria-label="Outline of the written audit, not client results">
        <div class="report-top"><img src="/logo.svg" alt="Wardith" width="140" height="26" /><span>Your audit / Report outline</span></div>
        <h3>Your business,<br />through the eyes of AI.</h3>
        <ol class="report-contents">
          <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Where you appear</strong><p>The questions asked. The answers recorded. The businesses mentioned.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><strong>What’s getting in the way</strong><p>Website access, conflicting business facts and gaps in your content.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><strong>What to do next</strong><p>Practical priorities, supported by what we found.</p></div></li>
        </ol><div class="report-bottom"><span>Evidence first. Recommendations second.</span><span>W / 01</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section proof-section"><div class="wrap proof-grid"><div><p class="section-label">Our work, in the open</p><h2>We tested ourselves.<br /><em>Then changed<br />our name.</em></h2><p>Our first audit found a problem with our own business name. We published the findings, including the failure.</p><a class="text-link" href="/ask-your-ai/self-audit/">Read the original audit <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="proof-record"><div class="big-number">228<span>recorded answers</span></div><div class="proof-numbers"><p><strong>10</strong> questions</p><p><strong>4</strong> assistants</p></div><p class="proof-caption">Our original self-audit, under the name Noven. Historical research, not a promise of client results.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap pathway-grid"><div><p class="section-label">Only the work you need</p><h2>A clear next step.<br />At every stage.</h2><p>Start with the diagnosis. Decide what follows when you have the evidence.</p><a class="text-link" href="/pricing/">All prices and inclusions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><ol class="service-path"><li><span class="path-number">01</span><div><h3>Find out</h3><p>The audit explains where you stand and what needs attention.</p></div><span class="path-price">{money(audit.price)}<small>one-off</small></span></li><li><span class="path-number">02</span><div><h3>Put it right</h3><p>Foundation fixes agreed issues on your existing website.</p></div><span class="path-price">{money(foundation.price)}<small>one-off</small></span></li><li><span class="path-number">03</span><div><h3>Keep checking</h3><p>Optional monthly work as the answers and your business change.</p></div><span class="path-price">From {money(maintain.price)}<small>per month</small></span></li></ol></div></section>

  <section class="section founder-section"><div class="wrap founder-grid"><img class="founder-home" src={business.founderPhoto!} alt="Kieran Smith, founder of Wardith" width="880" height="1100" loading="lazy" /><div><p class="section-label">The person behind the report</p><h2>You work<br />directly with Kieran.</h2><p>I run Wardith from the Wirral, working with service businesses across the UK. When you email, I’m the person who replies and does the work.</p><p>AI recommendations can’t be guaranteed. What I can give you is a clear record of what happened, an explanation of what we can influence, and prices you can see before you start.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">More about Wardith <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>

  <section class="section compact-section"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="section-label">A closer look</p><h2>Evidence you can inspect.</h2></div><div><details class="disclose"><summary>Is this right for my business?</summary><p>Wardith is for UK service businesses whose customers research and compare before buying: accountants, solicitors, clinics, consultancies and agencies. It is less useful if customers buy on impulse or you already have more work than you want.</p></details><details class="disclose"><summary>Can you guarantee an AI recommendation?</summary><p>No. Assistants control their answers, and those answers change. We test what they say and work on the business information and website issues we can influence.</p></details><details class="disclose"><summary>See this website’s machine-readable facts</summary><p>Structured data gives machines an explicit record alongside the page’s content. This is the same record published in this page’s source.</p><Code caption="Wardith’s published business record" label="Wardith organisation JSON-LD" data={orgSchema} /></details><a class="text-link faq-link" href="/faq/">More questions, answered <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
</Base>
